==Strategy==
This stage is a fairly tough one in general and probably one of the hardest in the entirety of The Aku Realms. Mexico starts off with a swarm of Gabriels to give you money, which will be necessary later on as the rest of this stage is very punishing if you run out. Upon hitting the enemy base, additional Gabriels will swarm out, along with Sunfish Jones and a Fallen Bear. Every 10 seconds, an additional Fallen Bear will enter the fray until 5 bears have been let out, so make sure you take out each bear as soon as possible, just make sure to do this while keeping out for Jones, the swarm of Gabriels and your cash.

A seal level of 40 is the bare minimum for this stage, as at this level Manic Eraser can survive an attack from a Fallen Bear. Though given this stage's difficulty relative to the others, it may also be a good idea to save this one for last. This stage can also be inconsistent, requiring luck for non-guaranteed [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercers]] such as [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]] to destroy the Fallen Bears' [[Shield]]s, and demanding another layer of luck to prevent the bears' [[Death Surge]]s from sniping your attackers.

If using Aku Researcher (preferably in [[True Form]]), expect this stage to take a few tries, as his low chance of Shield Piercing and the Gabriels constantly getting in the way make using him tricky. However, if an opening is found and a couple of their Shields are pierced, push the now-vulnerable bears back using the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast]] Cannon and let him loose on the rest. If you have them, [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]], despite not outranging the Fallen Bears, may be better here as they can snipe the bears using the Gabriels as stepping stones. With the horde of Gabriels that spawn upon base hit, this isn't very difficult to take advantage of. Their Area Attack means they can even break multiple Shields at once, and their Surge Immunity ensures they won't get killed from the Death Surges made by Fallen Bears.

[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and Talented [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]] will both help in this stage, although you do need some luck for the latter to Dodge. [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge-immune units]] are also helpful, such as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Actress Cat (Special Cat)|Beefcake Cat]], who is Surge-immune, capable of outranging the Fallen Bears, and quite tanky overall with maxed Talents. He also has Area Attack, helping you get rid of the enemies quite fast, especially with Strengthen.

